% Test cases for the PAP policy (pap.le): synthetic claims, one or two per
% criterion of LCD L33718 and per error category of the audits (OIG
% A-04-17-04056 and A-05-21-00036, CERT), each stating only what its record
% shows. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so
% "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and
% what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base pap cases includes these resources:
    pap.

the knowledge base pap cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for a CPAP: every criterion and every
% documentation requirement in the record.
scenario initial_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    Ann received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    the order for the CPAP device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the CPAP device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the CPAP device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the CPAP device includes order date.
    the order for the CPAP device includes description of the item.
    the order for the CPAP device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the CPAP device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the CPAP device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the CPAP device.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A mild apnea (AHI 9, 12 events) with a documented symptom: criterion B2.
scenario mild_with_hypertension is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ben.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 2.
    Ben has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ben had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ben was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ben is home sleep test.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ben is 9.
    the sleep test of Ben recorded 12 events.
    the medical record of Ben documents hypertension.
    Ben received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The same apnea without a documented symptom: not reasonable and necessary.
scenario mild_without_symptoms is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 2.
    Ben has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ben had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ben was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ben is home sleep test.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ben is 9.
    the sleep test of Ben recorded 12 events.
    Ben received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% The clinical evaluation came after the sleep test: criterion A fails.
scenario evaluation_after_test is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Cy has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Cy had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the sleep test of Cy was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Cy is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Cy is 40.
    the sleep test of Cy recorded 200 events.
    Cy received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    rn expects answers [].

% A home sleep test run by the DME supplier itself (Policy Article A52467).
scenario supplier_ran_the_test is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Dee has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Dee had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Dee was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Dee is home sleep test.
    the sleep test of Dee was performed by the DME supplier.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Dee is 40.
    the sleep test of Dee recorded 200 events.
    Dee received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    rn expects answers [].

% Month 4: re-evaluated on day 45, improved, 78 percent adherence.
scenario month_4_adherent is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Eve.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    Eve has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Eve had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Eve was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Eve is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Eve is 22.
    the sleep test of Eve recorded 140 events.
    Eve received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Eve had an in-person clinical re-evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-04-15.
    the re-evaluation of Eve on 2026-04-15 documents that the symptoms of obstructive sleep apnea are improved.
    Eve used the CPAP device at least four hours per night on 78 percent of nights during a consecutive thirty day period within the first three months.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Month 4 with 55 percent adherence: continued coverage fails.
scenario month_4_not_adherent is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Eve.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    Eve has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Eve had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Eve was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Eve is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Eve is 22.
    the sleep test of Eve recorded 140 events.
    Eve received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Eve had an in-person clinical re-evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-04-15.
    the re-evaluation of Eve on 2026-04-15 documents that the symptoms of obstructive sleep apnea are improved.
    Eve used the CPAP device at least four hours per night on 55 percent of nights during a consecutive thirty day period within the first three months.
    rn expects answers [].

% A late re-evaluation (day 120): coverage resumes from its date — the June
% claim is not covered, the August claim is.
scenario late_reevaluation is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Fay.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    claim 2 is for the CPAP device.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-08-01.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 6.
    Fay has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Fay had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Fay was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Fay is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Fay is 22.
    the sleep test of Fay recorded 140 events.
    Fay received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Fay had an in-person clinical re-evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-06-29.
    the re-evaluation of Fay on 2026-06-29 documents that the symptoms of obstructive sleep apnea are improved.
    Fay used the CPAP device at least four hours per night on 80 percent of nights during a consecutive thirty day period within the first three months.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A bi-level device with back-up rate (E0471) for OSA: no rule covers it.
scenario e0471_for_osa is:
    claim 1 is for the bilevel device.
    the HCPCS code of the bilevel device is "E0471".
    the bilevel device is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Gus has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    rn expects answers [].

% Accessories: a full face mask cushion (A7031, 1 per month) — one for a
% one-month supply is within the usual maximum, three are not.
scenario accessory_quantity is:
    claim 1 is for the mask cushion.
    the HCPCS code of the mask cushion is "A7031".
    the mask cushion is an accessory of the CPAP device.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-01.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 1.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 2 is for the mask cushions.
    the HCPCS code of the mask cushions is "A7031".
    the mask cushions is an accessory of the CPAP device.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-04-01.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 3.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    Ann received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the CPAP device.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    Ann received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    the order for the CPAP device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the CPAP device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the CPAP device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the CPAP device includes order date.
    the order for the CPAP device includes description of the item.
    the order for the CPAP device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the CPAP device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the CPAP device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the CPAP device"]].

% A refill of supplies ordered 45 days before the supply runs out, and one in
% time.
scenario refill_timing is:
    claim 1 is for the filters.
    the HCPCS code of the filters is "A7038".
    the filters is an accessory of the CPAP device.
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-25.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 2.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the current supply of the filters is expected to end on 2026-06-01.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the filters on 2026-04-15.
    the filters was delivered on 2026-05-25.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the filters.
    the order for the filters is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the filters is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the filters includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the filters includes order date.
    the order for the filters includes description of the item.
    the order for the filters includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the filters includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the filters was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the filters is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the medical record documents continued need for the filters on 2026-04-10.
    the record documents continued use of the filters on 2026-04-10.
    the HCPCS code of the CPAP device is "E0601".
    the CPAP device is furnished to Ann.
    the CPAP device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    Ann received instruction from the supplier in the use and care of the CPAP device.
    pay expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
